From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:50:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 084/117] dt-bindings: net: brcmfmac: Add D111 BCM4355 Wi-Fi

D111 integrates BCM4355 behind PCIe with board-specific wake and power
sequencing. Add a specific compatible followed by the generic BCM4355
PCI fallback so brcmfmac retains generic device identity while platform
power control can select D111 behavior.

Relax the device-wake description because D111 asserts the signal before
rail enable, unlike J172.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: 90b8bb726505484fb5ff26673ef8672e6241d238
---
 .../bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml           | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
index d099b591d..9e31844a4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/brcm,bcm4329-fmac.yaml
@@ -56,6 +56,9 @@ properties:
           - pci14e4,4433  # BCM4387
           - pci14e4,4434  # BCM4388
           - pci14e4,449d  # BCM43752
+      - items:
+          - const: apple,d111-bcm4355-wifi
+          - const: pci14e4,43dc
 
   reg:
     description: SDIO function number for the device (for most cases
@@ -91,8 +94,8 @@ properties:
   device-wake-gpios:
     maxItems: 1
     description:
-      Host-to-device wake signal held inactive while Apple PCIe modules are
-      powered for initial enumeration.
+      Host-to-device wake signal. Its required level during initial PCIe
+      enumeration depends on the Apple module integration.
 
   vdd-supply:
     description: Power supply for the Wi-Fi device.
